{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/767463-pittsburgh-pa-looking-for-local-game","id":767463,"title":"Pittsburgh- PA Looking for Local Game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-16T17:28:09-08:00","id":767463,"title":"Pittsburgh- PA Looking for Local Game","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My girlfriend and I just moved into the Hampton Township area. Looking for a weekly game of some sort with room for one or two players. Experienced in new WoD (Preference for Changeling or Geist but open for any), Scion, Shadowrun, Pathfinder, and Hero System. We've been gaming for about 5+ years.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9445-wisetiki","name":"Wisetiki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T06:35:55-08:00","id":792139,"title":"","content":"I'm in verona and would totally be up for a game of anything new wod (CofD). I've been digging into the changeling core, I've not looked at geist yet though!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10432-hexxentanz","name":"hexxentanz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T14:51:42-08:00","id":797517,"title":"","content":"My partner and I live in the Pittsburgh area and are currently trying to decide what to do about a group. We had one group going for about four years but eventually everyone kind of went off in their own direction. I'm currently most excited (read: obsessed) about Mage 2e, but I like most of the CoD games and I've also run Demon the Descent in addition to Mage 1e. My partner has run Vampire the Requiem and Geist games for our old group.<br /> <br /> Outside of CoD, we've got a variety of games we're into, lately leaning more heavily toward indie RPG systems (Fate, Burning Wheel, the &quot;World&quot; games, DCC) for me and foreign games (Double Cross, Tenra Bansho Zero, Shinobi Gami) for my partner, although we have been known to dungeon a dragon or war in the stars from time to time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10592-phlox","name":"Phlox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T16:45:58-08:00","id":799858,"title":"","content":"Most my experience was STing V:TR and W:TF, I moved away from my old group, (as did the group scatter to different spots around the country). I've not played any mage yet, but I figure since it's very close to 2e, I'd prefer to wait until then before taking the plunge. Promethian has that same issue for me as well. Reading the CofD book is really making me interested in a core mortals game or hunter game. Really the only CofD games I'm not familiar with at all (outside of mage) is geist/mummy/demon. If everyone's into one of those games, I'll def snag a copy off of drive through and check it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10432-hexxentanz","name":"hexxentanz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T19:44:46-08:00","id":800050,"title":"","content":"I've also been reading CofD's advance PDF and thinking that it might be a good idea to start off with mortals. I've been reading it straight through, trying to get into the habit, since I feel like I've surrounded by books I sometimes <i>use, </i>but never really read. A mortals game could be a good place from which to explore the other game lines, introduce concepts from different games, see what sticks. And if those lines are explored, you can always fall back to the mortals after a chronicle ends or if it isn't a good fit. (I also just want to get into some David Lynch-style weirdness with some mortal characters.)<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if the OP has checked back in since the thread started, but it seems like there are at least some people in the area who are still looking to put together a CofD game. I guess the next step would be to discuss further via PM? And maybe eventually arrange a game shop, coffee shop or other neutral place meeting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10592-phlox","name":"Phlox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T14:54:54-08:00","id":800755,"title":"","content":"Agreed. I'm about to ST an online god machine game (I've only read the wellington school story, so I'll keep myself from reading the other content. I figure that there's a lot of new rules in this new edition, so I agree that mortals would be a good starting point. While we don't have to use the god machine chronicles themselves, I do like the format of the 2-4 session scope games, which could be a good framework to use if we make a custom story. It'd get us acclimated to all the second edition stuff without throwing supernatural society/abilities on top of it all. I'll send you a PM, (I'm sending this here in case the OP checks on this again, or if there's other pittsburghers who see this)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10432-hexxentanz","name":"hexxentanz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T15:47:45-08:00","id":803394,"title":"","content":"Replied to your PM, and PM'd the OP with you copied. Oh, and don't worry about reading further in the book. I have an idea or two for a mystery plot - if I were to wind up running something - and we generally make up our own stuff unless we're doing standard fantasy stuff like Dungeon Crawl Classics or D&amp;D.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10592-phlox","name":"Phlox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}